          {
            "heading": "Part E: Aadi ki kahani ka jawab",
            "headingHinglish": "Part E: Aadi ki kahani ka jawab",
            "body": "Wapas academy chalte hain. Mr. Bedi ne Example 1 mein dekha ki 108 km/h = 30 m/s.\n\n**Example 12: Pitch par gend ka time**\n\nPitch 20 m lambi hai. Agar gend ki speed 30 m/s hi rahe, to 20 m kitne time mein?\n\n- Time = distance ÷ speed = 20 m ÷ 30 m/s = **0.67 s** (lagbhag, do decimal tak)\n\n**Jaanch:** 30 m/s × 0.67 s = 20.1 m ≈ 20 m ✅\n\nYani batsman ke paas sochne ke liye ek second se bhi kam. Isiliye tez gend khelna mushkil hota hai.\n\n**Aur Aadi ka doosra sawaal: 108 km/h aur average speed ek hi cheez hai?**\n\nMr. Bedi ne samjhaya, \"Speed gun gend ke haath se chhootne ke thik baad ki speed dikhati hai. Hum yahan **saral banane** ke liye maan rahe hain ki gend poori pitch par wahi 30 m/s se gayi. Par asliyat mein hawa gend ko thoda rokti hai aur pitch par uchhalne se bhi gend ki speed kam ho jaati hai.\"\n\nMaan lo stopwatch se naapa gaya ki 20 m tay karne mein asal mein 0.72 s lage.\n\n- Average speed = 20 m ÷ 0.72 s = **27.8 m/s** (lagbhag)\n- Km/h mein: 27.78 m/s × 3.6 = **100 km/h** (lagbhag)\n\n**Jaanch:** 27.78 m/s × 0.72 s = 20 m ✅\n\nTo speed gun ka 108 km/h gend ke chhootne ke time ki speed thi, aur poori pitch ka **average speed** thoda kam, lagbhag 100 km/h, nikla. Dono alag cheezein hain: ek \"us pal ki speed\", doosra \"poori doori ÷ poora time\". Ye \"us pal ki speed\" wali baat kitni gehri hai, wo aage ki class mein; abhi bas itna yaad rakho ki average speed poori yatra ka hota hai. Aur ye bhi dhyan rahe: speed gun ne **speed** dikhayi, direction nahi, to wo speed hai, velocity nahi.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Wapas academy chalte hain. Mr. Bedi ne Example 1 mein dekha ki 108 km/h = 30 m/s.\n\n**Example 12: Pitch par gend ka time**\n\nPitch 20 m lambi hai. Agar gend ki speed 30 m/s hi rahe, to 20 m kitne time mein?\n\n- Time = distance ÷ speed = 20 m ÷ 30 m/s = **0.67 s** (lagbhag, do decimal tak)\n\n**Jaanch:** 30 m/s × 0.67 s = 20.1 m ≈ 20 m ✅\n\nYani batsman ke paas sochne ke liye ek second se bhi kam. Isiliye tez gend khelna mushkil hota hai.\n\n**Aur Aadi ka doosra sawaal: 108 km/h aur average speed ek hi cheez hai?**\n\nMr. Bedi ne samjhaya, \"Speed gun gend ke haath se chhootne ke thik baad ki speed dikhati hai. Hum yahan **saral banane** ke liye maan rahe hain ki gend poori pitch par wahi 30 m/s se gayi. Par asliyat mein hawa gend ko thoda rokti hai aur pitch par uchhalne se bhi gend ki speed kam ho jaati hai.\"\n\nMaan lo stopwatch se naapa gaya ki 20 m tay karne mein asal mein 0.72 s lage.\n\n- Average speed = 20 m ÷ 0.72 s = **27.8 m/s** (lagbhag)\n- Km/h mein: 27.78 m/s × 3.6 = **100 km/h** (lagbhag)\n\n**Jaanch:** 27.78 m/s × 0.72 s = 20 m ✅\n\nTo speed gun ka 108 km/h gend ke chhootne ke time ki speed thi, aur poori pitch ka **average speed** thoda kam, lagbhag 100 km/h, nikla. Dono alag cheezein hain: ek \"us pal ki speed\", doosra \"poori doori ÷ poora time\". Ye \"us pal ki speed\" wali baat kitni gehri hai, wo aage ki class mein; abhi bas itna yaad rakho ki average speed poori yatra ka hota hai. Aur ye bhi dhyan rahe: speed gun ne **speed** dikhayi, direction nahi, to wo speed hai, velocity nahi."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Part F: Ek mushkil sawaal: train aur platform",
            "headingHinglish": "Part F: Ek mushkil sawaal: train aur platform",
            "body": "**Example 13: Train ka platform cross karna**\n\n200 m lambi train 90 km/h ki constant speed se 300 m lambe platform ko poora cross karti hai. Kitna time lagega?\n\nTrain \"platform cross kar chuki\" tab maani jaati hai jab uska **aakhri dabba** bhi platform se bahar ho jaye. Isliye train ko platform ki length **plus** apni length, dono tay karni padti hai.\n\n```\n   Shuru:    [=== train 200 m ===]|---- platform 300 m ----|\n\n   Ant:                           |---- platform 300 m ----|[=== train ===]\n```\n\n> **Figure 3.3** – Train ka engine platform ke shuru par aaya aur aakhri dabba platform ke ant se nikla: total doori = train ki length + platform ki length.\n\n- Total distance = 200 m + 300 m = **500 m**\n- Speed = 90 km/h × 5/18 = 90 ÷ 18 × 5 = **25 m/s**\n- Time = 500 m ÷ 25 m/s = **20 s**\n\n**Jaanch:** 25 m/s × 20 s = 500 m ✅",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Example 13: Train ka platform cross karna**\n\n200 m lambi train 90 km/h ki constant speed se 300 m lambe platform ko poora cross karti hai. Kitna time lagega?\n\nTrain \"platform cross kar chuki\" tab maani jaati hai jab uska **aakhri dabba** bhi platform se bahar ho jaye. Isliye train ko platform ki length **plus** apni length, dono tay karni padti hai.\n\n```\n   Shuru:    [=== train 200 m ===]|---- platform 300 m ----|\n\n   Ant:                           |---- platform 300 m ----|[=== train ===]\n```\n\n> **Figure 3.3** – Train ka engine platform ke shuru par aaya aur aakhri dabba platform ke ant se nikla: total doori = train ki length + platform ki length.\n\n- Total distance = 200 m + 300 m = **500 m**\n- Speed = 90 km/h × 5/18 = 90 ÷ 18 × 5 = **25 m/s**\n- Time = 500 m ÷ 25 m/s = **20 s**\n\n**Jaanch:** 25 m/s × 20 s = 500 m ✅"
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti 1: Do speeds ka seedha average**\n\n30 km/h aur 60 km/h ke liye (30 + 60) ÷ 2 = 45 likhna galat hai jab doori barabar ho. Sahi: total distance ÷ total time = 120 ÷ 3 = 40 km/h (Example 6).\n\n**Galti 2: km/h aur m/s ko mix karna**\n\nDistance 500 m aur speed 90 km/h ho to seedha 500 ÷ 90 mat karo. Pehle ek hi unit mein lao: 90 km/h = 25 m/s, phir 500 ÷ 25 = 20 s.\n\n**Galti 3: Velocity ke liye distance lena**\n\nVelocity mein **displacement** aata hai. Round trip mein distance 80 m tha, par displacement 0, to average velocity 0 (Example 10), 1 m/s nahi.\n\n**Galti 4: Halt ko total time mein na jodna**\n\nBus ke 30 min ke halt ko bhool kar 150 ÷ 2.5 = 60 km/h likha, sahi 50 km/h hai (Example 8).\n\n**Galti 5: Sochna ki velocity negative nahi ho sakti**\n\nNegative velocity ka matlab sirf ulti direction hai. −2 m/s ka matlab 2 m/s west ki taraf, jab east positive ho. Speed hamesha positive ya zero hoti hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti 1: Do speeds ka seedha average**\n\n30 km/h aur 60 km/h ke liye (30 + 60) ÷ 2 = 45 likhna galat hai jab doori barabar ho. Sahi: total distance ÷ total time = 120 ÷ 3 = 40 km/h (Example 6).\n\n**Galti 2: km/h aur m/s ko mix karna**\n\nDistance 500 m aur speed 90 km/h ho to seedha 500 ÷ 90 mat karo. Pehle ek hi unit mein lao: 90 km/h = 25 m/s, phir 500 ÷ 25 = 20 s.\n\n**Galti 3: Velocity ke liye distance lena**\n\nVelocity mein **displacement** aata hai. Round trip mein distance 80 m tha, par displacement 0, to average velocity 0 (Example 10), 1 m/s nahi.\n\n**Galti 4: Halt ko total time mein na jodna**\n\nBus ke 30 min ke halt ko bhool kar 150 ÷ 2.5 = 60 km/h likha, sahi 50 km/h hai (Example 8).\n\n**Galti 5: Sochna ki velocity negative nahi ho sakti**\n\nNegative velocity ka matlab sirf ulti direction hai. −2 m/s ka matlab 2 m/s west ki taraf, jab east positive ho. Speed hamesha positive ya zero hoti hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Speed = distance ÷ time**; scalar; SI unit **m/s**. \"Ek second mein kitni doori.\"\n- **1 km/h = 5/18 m/s**; km/h se m/s ke liye 3.6 se bhaag, m/s se km/h ke liye 3.6 se guna. Jaise 108 km/h = 30 m/s.\n- **Uniform speed:** barabar time mein barabar doori. **Variable speed:** speed badalti rehti hai.\n- **Average speed = total distance ÷ total time** (halt bhi time mein). Ye do speeds ka seedha average nahi hai: 60 km at 30 km/h aur 60 km at 60 km/h ka average 40 km/h.\n- **Velocity = displacement ÷ time**; vector; seedhi line mein + ya − ho sakti hai.\n- **Average velocity = total displacement ÷ total time.** Round trip mein 0, par average speed 0 nahi.\n- Speed aur velocity ki magnitude tab barabar jab seedhi line mein bina wapas mude chalein.\n- **Speedometer** speed dikhata hai, **odometer** ab tak tay hui doori.\n- Approximate speeds: chalna 1.4 m/s, cycle 5 m/s, car 25 m/s, awaaz 340 m/s, roshni 3 × 10⁸ m/s.\n- **Kahani ka jawab:** 108 km/h = 30 m/s; 20 m ka time = 0.67 s; poori pitch ka average speed thoda kam (lagbhag 100 km/h agar 0.72 s lage).",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Speed = distance ÷ time**; scalar; SI unit **m/s**. \"Ek second mein kitni doori.\"\n- **1 km/h = 5/18 m/s**; km/h se m/s ke liye 3.6 se bhaag, m/s se km/h ke liye 3.6 se guna. Jaise 108 km/h = 30 m/s.\n- **Uniform speed:** barabar time mein barabar doori. **Variable speed:** speed badalti rehti hai.\n- **Average speed = total distance ÷ total time** (halt bhi time mein). Ye do speeds ka seedha average nahi hai: 60 km at 30 km/h aur 60 km at 60 km/h ka average 40 km/h.\n- **Velocity = displacement ÷ time**; vector; seedhi line mein + ya − ho sakti hai.\n- **Average velocity = total displacement ÷ total time.** Round trip mein 0, par average speed 0 nahi.\n- Speed aur velocity ki magnitude tab barabar jab seedhi line mein bina wapas mude chalein.\n- **Speedometer** speed dikhata hai, **odometer** ab tak tay hui doori.\n- Approximate speeds: chalna 1.4 m/s, cycle 5 m/s, car 25 m/s, awaaz 340 m/s, roshni 3 × 10⁸ m/s.\n- **Kahani ka jawab:** 108 km/h = 30 m/s; 20 m ka time = 0.67 s; poori pitch ka average speed thoda kam (lagbhag 100 km/h agar 0.72 s lage)."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. A cyclist covers 1.8 km in 6 minutes. Find her speed in m/s and in km/h.\n\n2. Convert (a) 54 km/h into m/s and (b) 8 m/s into km/h.\n\n3. A bus moves at a constant 20 m/s. How much time will it take to cover 3 km? Give the answer in seconds and in minutes.\n\n4. Sound travels at about 340 m/s in air. How far does it travel in 4 s?\n\n5. A car travels 100 km at 50 km/h and then another 100 km at 100 km/h. Find the average speed for the whole journey. Why is it not 75 km/h?\n\n6. A student walks 1.2 km in 20 min, rests for 10 min, and then walks 0.6 km in 10 min. Find the average speed for the whole trip in km/h and in m/s.\n\n7. On a straight track, a runner goes 100 m east in 20 s and then 40 m west in 10 s. Find (a) the average speed and (b) the average velocity for the whole 30 s.\n\n8. A 150 m long train crosses a 450 m long bridge at 72 km/h. How long does it take to cross the bridge completely?\n\n9. A runner completes one full lap of a 400 m circular track in 80 s, ending where she started. Find her average speed and her average velocity.\n\n10. State True or False:\n    (a) Speed can be negative.\n    (b) Velocity can be negative.\n    (c) Average velocity of a round trip is zero.\n    (d) For equal distances at 20 km/h and 30 km/h, the average speed is 25 km/h.\n    (e) The speedometer of a car shows the total distance it has covered.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. Distance = 1.8 km = 1800 m, time = 6 min = 360 s.\n   Speed = 1800 m ÷ 360 s = **5 m/s**. Km/h mein: 5 × 3.6 = **18 km/h**.\n   Jaanch: 5 m/s × 360 s = 1800 m ✅\n\n2. (a) 54 × 5/18 = 54 ÷ 18 × 5 = 3 × 5 = **15 m/s**.\n   (b) 8 × 18/5 = 8 × 3.6 = **28.8 km/h**.\n   Jaanch: 15 × 3.6 = 54 ✅ aur 28.8 ÷ 3.6 = 8 ✅\n\n3. Distance = 3 km = 3000 m. Time = 3000 m ÷ 20 m/s = **150 s** = **2.5 min**.\n   Jaanch: 20 m/s × 150 s = 3000 m ✅\n\n4. Distance = 340 m/s × 4 s = **1360 m** (lagbhag 1.36 km).\n   Jaanch: 1360 ÷ 4 = 340 m/s ✅\n\n5. Time 1 = 100 km ÷ 50 km/h = 2 h. Time 2 = 100 km ÷ 100 km/h = 1 h.\n   Total distance = 200 km, total time = 3 h.\n   Average speed = 200 ÷ 3 = **66.7 km/h** (lagbhag).\n   75 isliye nahi: gaadi ne kam speed par zyada time (2 h) bitaya, to average 50 ke paas rehta hai.\n   Jaanch: 66.7 km/h × 3 h ≈ 200 km ✅\n\n6. Total distance = 1.2 + 0.6 = 1.8 km. Total time = 20 + 10 + 10 = 40 min = 2/3 h (rest bhi shamil).\n   Average speed = 1.8 ÷ (2/3) = **2.7 km/h**. m/s mein: 2.7 ÷ 3.6 = **0.75 m/s**.\n   Jaanch: 1800 m ÷ 2400 s = 0.75 m/s ✅\n\n7. (a) Total distance = 100 + 40 = 140 m, total time = 20 + 10 = 30 s. Average speed = 140 ÷ 30 = **4.67 m/s** (lagbhag).\n   (b) Displacement = 100 m east − 40 m west = 60 m east. Average velocity = 60 ÷ 30 = **2 m/s east ki taraf**.\n   Jaanch: 2 m/s × 30 s = 60 m ✅\n\n8. Total distance = 150 + 450 = 600 m. Speed = 72 × 5/18 = 20 m/s.\n   Time = 600 ÷ 20 = **30 s**.\n   Jaanch: 20 m/s × 30 s = 600 m ✅\n\n9. Distance = 400 m, time = 80 s: average speed = 400 ÷ 80 = **5 m/s**.\n   Wo wahin pahunchi jahan se chali thi, to displacement = 0 aur average velocity = 0 ÷ 80 = **0 m/s**.\n   Jaanch: speed 5 m/s ≠ 0, par velocity 0 ✅\n\n10. (a) **False** ❌. Speed distance se banti hai, wo negative nahi hoti.\n    (b) **True** ✅. Negative velocity ulti direction batati hai.\n    (c) **True** ✅. Round trip mein displacement 0 hota hai.\n    (d) **False** ❌. Maan lo har taraf d km: time = d/20 + d/30 = d/12 h, total distance 2d, to average = 2d ÷ (d/12) = **24 km/h**, 25 nahi.\n    (e) **False** ❌. Speedometer abhi ki speed dikhata hai; total distance odometer dikhata hai.\n\n---\n\nAb aap jaante ho ki speed, average speed aur velocity mein kya farak hai, aur ek bhi yatra ko total distance, total displacement aur total time se kaise naapna hai. Agli baar kisi car ya train mein baithoge to speedometer ko dekh kar sochna: \"ye speed hai ya velocity?\"\n\n**Aage kya?** Aadi ki delivery 108 km/h par chhooti thi, par pitch ke ant tak aate-aate speed kam ho gayi. Aur bowling action ke us chhote se pal mein gend ki speed 30 m/s tak kaise pahunchi? **Agar speed hi badalti jaye, to kya hota hai?** Ye hum Topic 4 mein dekhenge.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. A cyclist covers 1.8 km in 6 minutes. Find her speed in m/s and in km/h.\n\n2. Convert (a) 54 km/h into m/s and (b) 8 m/s into km/h.\n\n3. A bus moves at a constant 20 m/s. How much time will it take to cover 3 km? Give the answer in seconds and in minutes.\n\n4. Sound travels at about 340 m/s in air. How far does it travel in 4 s?\n\n5. A car travels 100 km at 50 km/h and then another 100 km at 100 km/h. Find the average speed for the whole journey. Why is it not 75 km/h?\n\n6. A student walks 1.2 km in 20 min, rests for 10 min, and then walks 0.6 km in 10 min. Find the average speed for the whole trip in km/h and in m/s.\n\n7. On a straight track, a runner goes 100 m east in 20 s and then 40 m west in 10 s. Find (a) the average speed and (b) the average velocity for the whole 30 s.\n\n8. A 150 m long train crosses a 450 m long bridge at 72 km/h. How long does it take to cross the bridge completely?\n\n9. A runner completes one full lap of a 400 m circular track in 80 s, ending where she started. Find her average speed and her average velocity.\n\n10. State True or False:\n    (a) Speed can be negative.\n    (b) Velocity can be negative.\n    (c) Average velocity of a round trip is zero.\n    (d) For equal distances at 20 km/h and 30 km/h, the average speed is 25 km/h.\n    (e) The speedometer of a car shows the total distance it has covered.\n\n### Answers\n\n1. Distance = 1.8 km = 1800 m, time = 6 min = 360 s.\n   Speed = 1800 m ÷ 360 s = **5 m/s**. Km/h mein: 5 × 3.6 = **18 km/h**.\n   Jaanch: 5 m/s × 360 s = 1800 m ✅\n\n2. (a) 54 × 5/18 = 54 ÷ 18 × 5 = 3 × 5 = **15 m/s**.\n   (b) 8 × 18/5 = 8 × 3.6 = **28.8 km/h**.\n   Jaanch: 15 × 3.6 = 54 ✅ aur 28.8 ÷ 3.6 = 8 ✅\n\n3. Distance = 3 km = 3000 m. Time = 3000 m ÷ 20 m/s = **150 s** = **2.5 min**.\n   Jaanch: 20 m/s × 150 s = 3000 m ✅\n\n4. Distance = 340 m/s × 4 s = **1360 m** (lagbhag 1.36 km).\n   Jaanch: 1360 ÷ 4 = 340 m/s ✅\n\n5. Time 1 = 100 km ÷ 50 km/h = 2 h. Time 2 = 100 km ÷ 100 km/h = 1 h.\n   Total distance = 200 km, total time = 3 h.\n   Average speed = 200 ÷ 3 = **66.7 km/h** (lagbhag).\n   75 isliye nahi: gaadi ne kam speed par zyada time (2 h) bitaya, to average 50 ke paas rehta hai.\n   Jaanch: 66.7 km/h × 3 h ≈ 200 km ✅\n\n6. Total distance = 1.2 + 0.6 = 1.8 km. Total time = 20 + 10 + 10 = 40 min = 2/3 h (rest bhi shamil).\n   Average speed = 1.8 ÷ (2/3) = **2.7 km/h**. m/s mein: 2.7 ÷ 3.6 = **0.75 m/s**.\n   Jaanch: 1800 m ÷ 2400 s = 0.75 m/s ✅\n\n7. (a) Total distance = 100 + 40 = 140 m, total time = 20 + 10 = 30 s. Average speed = 140 ÷ 30 = **4.67 m/s** (lagbhag).\n   (b) Displacement = 100 m east − 40 m west = 60 m east. Average velocity = 60 ÷ 30 = **2 m/s east ki taraf**.\n   Jaanch: 2 m/s × 30 s = 60 m ✅\n\n8. Total distance = 150 + 450 = 600 m. Speed = 72 × 5/18 = 20 m/s.\n   Time = 600 ÷ 20 = **30 s**.\n   Jaanch: 20 m/s × 30 s = 600 m ✅\n\n9. Distance = 400 m, time = 80 s: average speed = 400 ÷ 80 = **5 m/s**.\n   Wo wahin pahunchi jahan se chali thi, to displacement = 0 aur average velocity = 0 ÷ 80 = **0 m/s**.\n   Jaanch: speed 5 m/s ≠ 0, par velocity 0 ✅\n\n10. (a) **False** ❌. Speed distance se banti hai, wo negative nahi hoti.\n    (b) **True** ✅. Negative velocity ulti direction batati hai.\n    (c) **True** ✅. Round trip mein displacement 0 hota hai.\n    (d) **False** ❌. Maan lo har taraf d km: time = d/20 + d/30 = d/12 h, total distance 2d, to average = 2d ÷ (d/12) = **24 km/h**, 25 nahi.\n    (e) **False** ❌. Speedometer abhi ki speed dikhata hai; total distance odometer dikhata hai.\n\n---\n\nAb aap jaante ho ki speed, average speed aur velocity mein kya farak hai, aur ek bhi yatra ko total distance, total displacement aur total time se kaise naapna hai. Agli baar kisi car ya train mein baithoge to speedometer ko dekh kar sochna: \"ye speed hai ya velocity?\"\n\n**Aage kya?** Aadi ki delivery 108 km/h par chhooti thi, par pitch ke ant tak aate-aate speed kam ho gayi. Aur bowling action ke us chhote se pal mein gend ki speed 30 m/s tak kaise pahunchi? **Agar speed hi badalti jaye, to kya hota hai?** Ye hum Topic 4 mein dekhenge."
          }
