          {
            "heading": "Part D: Aage ki jhalak: fluid bhi pressure lagate hain",
            "headingHinglish": "Part D: Aage ki jhalak: fluid bhi pressure lagate hain",
            "body": "Ab tak humne solid ka pressure dekha. Par **fluids** (liquid aur gas) bhi pressure lagate hain, aur wo apne **bartan ki deewaron** par lagate hain. Gubbare mein hawa uski deewar ko bahar ki taraf dabati hai, aur paani ki tanki ki deewar par paani dabav daalta hai. Fluids ka pressure kaise kaam karta hai, ye hum aage ke topics mein dekhenge. Abhi bas ye yaad rakho ki **pressure sirf solid ki cheez nahi hai**.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ab tak humne solid ka pressure dekha. Par **fluids** (liquid aur gas) bhi pressure lagate hain, aur wo apne **bartan ki deewaron** par lagate hain. Gubbare mein hawa uski deewar ko bahar ki taraf dabati hai, aur paani ki tanki ki deewar par paani dabav daalta hai. Fluids ka pressure kaise kaam karta hai, ye hum aage ke topics mein dekhenge. Abhi bas ye yaad rakho ki **pressure sirf solid ki cheez nahi hai**."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "headingHinglish": "Aam galtiyan (bachke rehna)",
            "body": "**Galti 1: Force aur pressure ko ek hi samajhna.**\nForce (thrust) ka unit N hai, pressure ka unit Pa (N/m²) hai. Force kul dabav batata hai, pressure batata hai ki **har m² par** kitna dabav hai. Ek hi force alag-alag areas par alag pressure banata hai.\n\n**Galti 2: Area cm² mein rakhkar answer Pa mein likhna.**\nMisaal: 30 N ÷ 15 cm² = 2 **sahi nahi hai** (ye \"2 N/cm²\" hoga, Pa nahi). Sahi: 15 cm² = 0.0015 m², P = 30 N ÷ 0.0015 m² = **20000 Pa**.\n\n**Galti 3: cm² ko m² mein badalte waqt 100 se bhaag dena.**\n1 cm = 10⁻² m, to 1 cm² = 10⁻⁴ m² (10,000 se bhaag). Agar 100 se bhaage: 200 cm² ko 2 m² likh doge, jabki sahi 0.02 m² hai, aur pressure 100 guna galat aayega.\n\n**Galti 4: Sochna ki pressure sirf force par depend karta hai.**\nPressure = F ÷ A. Haathi ka force bahut zyada hai par uske pair chaude hain; ladki ki heel ka force kam hai par area bahut chhota hai, isliye uska pressure zyada nikla (Example 8).\n\n**Galti 5: Sochna ki chaude object ka force kam hota hai.**\nTractor ke chaude tyre ya camel ke chaude pair se force (weight) kam nahi hota. Force **wahi** rehta hai; bas wo badi jagah par fail jaata hai, isliye **pressure kam** hota hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "**Galti 1: Force aur pressure ko ek hi samajhna.**\nForce (thrust) ka unit N hai, pressure ka unit Pa (N/m²) hai. Force kul dabav batata hai, pressure batata hai ki **har m² par** kitna dabav hai. Ek hi force alag-alag areas par alag pressure banata hai.\n\n**Galti 2: Area cm² mein rakhkar answer Pa mein likhna.**\nMisaal: 30 N ÷ 15 cm² = 2 **sahi nahi hai** (ye \"2 N/cm²\" hoga, Pa nahi). Sahi: 15 cm² = 0.0015 m², P = 30 N ÷ 0.0015 m² = **20000 Pa**.\n\n**Galti 3: cm² ko m² mein badalte waqt 100 se bhaag dena.**\n1 cm = 10⁻² m, to 1 cm² = 10⁻⁴ m² (10,000 se bhaag). Agar 100 se bhaage: 200 cm² ko 2 m² likh doge, jabki sahi 0.02 m² hai, aur pressure 100 guna galat aayega.\n\n**Galti 4: Sochna ki pressure sirf force par depend karta hai.**\nPressure = F ÷ A. Haathi ka force bahut zyada hai par uske pair chaude hain; ladki ki heel ka force kam hai par area bahut chhota hai, isliye uska pressure zyada nikla (Example 8).\n\n**Galti 5: Sochna ki chaude object ka force kam hota hai.**\nTractor ke chaude tyre ya camel ke chaude pair se force (weight) kam nahi hota. Force **wahi** rehta hai; bas wo badi jagah par fail jaata hai, isliye **pressure kam** hota hai."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Quick Recap",
            "headingHinglish": "Quick Recap",
            "body": "- **Fluid** = liquid aur gas (jo beh sakte hain).\n- **Thrust** = sateh par seedha (perpendicular) lagne wala force. Unit: **N**.\n- Horizontal sateh par rakhe solid ka thrust uska **weight** hota hai: F = m × g.\n- **Pressure = thrust ÷ area**: **P = F ÷ A**.\n- SI unit: **pascal (Pa)**, 1 Pa = 1 N/m². 1 kPa = 1000 Pa, 1 bar = 10⁵ Pa.\n- Area ko hamesha **m²** mein badlo: 1 cm² = 10⁻⁴ m², 1 mm² = 10⁻⁶ m².\n- Area **chhota** to pressure **bada** (chaaku, keel, kulhaadi); area **bada** to pressure **chhota** (bag ke straps, tractor tyre, camel ke pair, snowshoes).\n- Force wahi rehta hai, sirf area badalne se pressure badal jaata hai.\n- Fluids bhi apne bartan ki deewaron par pressure lagate hain (aage dekhenge).",
            "bodyHinglish": "- **Fluid** = liquid aur gas (jo beh sakte hain).\n- **Thrust** = sateh par seedha (perpendicular) lagne wala force. Unit: **N**.\n- Horizontal sateh par rakhe solid ka thrust uska **weight** hota hai: F = m × g.\n- **Pressure = thrust ÷ area**: **P = F ÷ A**.\n- SI unit: **pascal (Pa)**, 1 Pa = 1 N/m². 1 kPa = 1000 Pa, 1 bar = 10⁵ Pa.\n- Area ko hamesha **m²** mein badlo: 1 cm² = 10⁻⁴ m², 1 mm² = 10⁻⁶ m².\n- Area **chhota** to pressure **bada** (chaaku, keel, kulhaadi); area **bada** to pressure **chhota** (bag ke straps, tractor tyre, camel ke pair, snowshoes).\n- Force wahi rehta hai, sirf area badalne se pressure badal jaata hai.\n- Fluids bhi apne bartan ki deewaron par pressure lagate hain (aage dekhenge)."
          },
          {
            "heading": "Practice Questions",
            "headingHinglish": "Practice Questions",
            "body": "1. What is the difference between thrust and pressure? State the SI unit of each.\n2. A force of 250 N acts at right angles on an area of 0.5 m². Find the pressure.\n3. A pressure of 8000 Pa acts on a surface of area 0.03 m². Find the thrust.\n4. A force of 900 N produces a pressure of 18000 Pa. Find the area on which it acts.\n5. A boy of mass 50 kg stands on both feet, with total contact area 0.05 m². Find the pressure he exerts on the floor (g = 10 m/s²). What happens to the pressure if he stands on one foot (area 0.025 m²)?\n6. A wooden block of mass 5 kg has dimensions 50 cm × 20 cm × 10 cm. Find the greatest and the least pressure it can exert on a table (g = 10 m/s²).\n7. A force of 12 N acts on an area of 6 cm². Find the pressure in pascal and in kPa.\n8. A sharp needle tip has area 0.2 mm². Find the pressure when it is pressed with a force of 4 N.\n9. Why do we use wide straps on a heavy school bag, and why is a nail pointed at one end?\n10. State true or false, with a reason: (a) A camel's wide feet reduce its weight. (b) 1 kPa = 1000 Pa. (c) If area is doubled and force stays the same, pressure becomes half. (d) 1 cm² = 10⁻² m².\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Thrust** sateh par seedha lagne wala force hai (SI unit **N**). **Pressure** har unit area par lagne wala thrust hai, P = F ÷ A (SI unit **Pa = N/m²**).\n\n2. P = 250 N ÷ 0.5 m² = **500 Pa**.\n   Jaanch: 500 Pa × 0.5 m² = 250 N ✅\n\n3. F = P × A = 8000 Pa × 0.03 m² = **240 N**.\n   Jaanch: 240 N ÷ 0.03 m² = 8000 Pa ✅\n\n4. A = F ÷ P = 900 N ÷ 18000 Pa = **0.05 m²**.\n   Jaanch: 900 N ÷ 0.05 m² = 18000 Pa ✅\n\n5. F = 50 kg × 10 m/s² = 500 N. Dono pair: P = 500 N ÷ 0.05 m² = **10000 Pa** (10 kPa). Ek pair: P = 500 N ÷ 0.025 m² = **20000 Pa**, yani pressure **doguna** ho jaata hai kyunki area aadha ho gaya.\n   Jaanch: 10000 × 0.05 = 500 N ✅, 20000 × 0.025 = 500 N ✅\n\n6. F = 5 kg × 10 m/s² = 50 N.\n   Sabse bada face: 50 cm × 20 cm = 1000 cm² = 0.1 m² (pressure sabse kam): P = 50 N ÷ 0.1 m² = **500 Pa** (least).\n   Sabse chhota face: 20 cm × 10 cm = 200 cm² = 0.02 m² (pressure sabse zyada): P = 50 N ÷ 0.02 m² = **2500 Pa** (greatest).\n   Jaanch: 500 × 0.1 = 50 N ✅, 2500 × 0.02 = 50 N ✅\n\n7. A = 6 cm² = 6 × 10⁻⁴ m². P = 12 N ÷ (6 × 10⁻⁴ m²) = **20000 Pa** = **20 kPa**.\n   Jaanch: 20000 × 6 × 10⁻⁴ = 12 N ✅\n\n8. A = 0.2 mm² = 0.2 × 10⁻⁶ m² = 2 × 10⁻⁷ m². P = 4 N ÷ (2 × 10⁻⁷ m²) = **2 × 10⁷ Pa**.\n   Jaanch: 2 × 10⁷ × 2 × 10⁻⁷ = 4 N ✅\n\n9. Chaude straps se bag ka weight badi jagah par fail jaata hai, area bada hone se pressure kam hota hai aur kandha kam dukhta hai. Keel ki nok ka area bahut chhota hota hai, isliye wahi force bahut zyada pressure banata hai aur nok lakdi mein ghus jaati hai.\n\n10. (a) **False** ❌. Weight wahi rehta hai; chaude pair se sirf pressure kam hota hai.\n    (b) **True** ✅. kilo ka matlab 1000.\n    (c) **True** ✅. P = F ÷ A, A doguna to P aadha.\n    (d) **False** ❌. 1 cm² = 10⁻⁴ m² (kyunki length ko 10⁻² se multiply karke square karte hain).\n\n---\n\nAb aap Anaya ko bata sakte ho ki tez chaaku se tamatar kyun kat gaya: force wahi, par area chhota, to pressure bada. Agli baar kuch bhi dabate ya chalte waqt sochna: \"Mera weight kitni badi jagah par fail raha hai?\"\n\n**Aage kya?** Ab dekhte hain ki paani ke andar pressure kitna hota hai aur wo gehraai ke saath kyun badhta hai.",
            "bodyHinglish": "1. What is the difference between thrust and pressure? State the SI unit of each.\n2. A force of 250 N acts at right angles on an area of 0.5 m². Find the pressure.\n3. A pressure of 8000 Pa acts on a surface of area 0.03 m². Find the thrust.\n4. A force of 900 N produces a pressure of 18000 Pa. Find the area on which it acts.\n5. A boy of mass 50 kg stands on both feet, with total contact area 0.05 m². Find the pressure he exerts on the floor (g = 10 m/s²). What happens to the pressure if he stands on one foot (area 0.025 m²)?\n6. A wooden block of mass 5 kg has dimensions 50 cm × 20 cm × 10 cm. Find the greatest and the least pressure it can exert on a table (g = 10 m/s²).\n7. A force of 12 N acts on an area of 6 cm². Find the pressure in pascal and in kPa.\n8. A sharp needle tip has area 0.2 mm². Find the pressure when it is pressed with a force of 4 N.\n9. Why do we use wide straps on a heavy school bag, and why is a nail pointed at one end?\n10. State true or false, with a reason: (a) A camel's wide feet reduce its weight. (b) 1 kPa = 1000 Pa. (c) If area is doubled and force stays the same, pressure becomes half. (d) 1 cm² = 10⁻² m².\n\n### Answers\n\n1. **Thrust** sateh par seedha lagne wala force hai (SI unit **N**). **Pressure** har unit area par lagne wala thrust hai, P = F ÷ A (SI unit **Pa = N/m²**).\n\n2. P = 250 N ÷ 0.5 m² = **500 Pa**.\n   Jaanch: 500 Pa × 0.5 m² = 250 N ✅\n\n3. F = P × A = 8000 Pa × 0.03 m² = **240 N**.\n   Jaanch: 240 N ÷ 0.03 m² = 8000 Pa ✅\n\n4. A = F ÷ P = 900 N ÷ 18000 Pa = **0.05 m²**.\n   Jaanch: 900 N ÷ 0.05 m² = 18000 Pa ✅\n\n5. F = 50 kg × 10 m/s² = 500 N. Dono pair: P = 500 N ÷ 0.05 m² = **10000 Pa** (10 kPa). Ek pair: P = 500 N ÷ 0.025 m² = **20000 Pa**, yani pressure **doguna** ho jaata hai kyunki area aadha ho gaya.\n   Jaanch: 10000 × 0.05 = 500 N ✅, 20000 × 0.025 = 500 N ✅\n\n6. F = 5 kg × 10 m/s² = 50 N.\n   Sabse bada face: 50 cm × 20 cm = 1000 cm² = 0.1 m² (pressure sabse kam): P = 50 N ÷ 0.1 m² = **500 Pa** (least).\n   Sabse chhota face: 20 cm × 10 cm = 200 cm² = 0.02 m² (pressure sabse zyada): P = 50 N ÷ 0.02 m² = **2500 Pa** (greatest).\n   Jaanch: 500 × 0.1 = 50 N ✅, 2500 × 0.02 = 50 N ✅\n\n7. A = 6 cm² = 6 × 10⁻⁴ m². P = 12 N ÷ (6 × 10⁻⁴ m²) = **20000 Pa** = **20 kPa**.\n   Jaanch: 20000 × 6 × 10⁻⁴ = 12 N ✅\n\n8. A = 0.2 mm² = 0.2 × 10⁻⁶ m² = 2 × 10⁻⁷ m². P = 4 N ÷ (2 × 10⁻⁷ m²) = **2 × 10⁷ Pa**.\n   Jaanch: 2 × 10⁷ × 2 × 10⁻⁷ = 4 N ✅\n\n9. Chaude straps se bag ka weight badi jagah par fail jaata hai, area bada hone se pressure kam hota hai aur kandha kam dukhta hai. Keel ki nok ka area bahut chhota hota hai, isliye wahi force bahut zyada pressure banata hai aur nok lakdi mein ghus jaati hai.\n\n10. (a) **False** ❌. Weight wahi rehta hai; chaude pair se sirf pressure kam hota hai.\n    (b) **True** ✅. kilo ka matlab 1000.\n    (c) **True** ✅. P = F ÷ A, A doguna to P aadha.\n    (d) **False** ❌. 1 cm² = 10⁻⁴ m² (kyunki length ko 10⁻² se multiply karke square karte hain).\n\n---\n\nAb aap Anaya ko bata sakte ho ki tez chaaku se tamatar kyun kat gaya: force wahi, par area chhota, to pressure bada. Agli baar kuch bhi dabate ya chalte waqt sochna: \"Mera weight kitni badi jagah par fail raha hai?\"\n\n**Aage kya?** Ab dekhte hain ki paani ke andar pressure kitna hota hai aur wo gehraai ke saath kyun badhta hai."
          }
