            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Pichle topic mein humne dekha ki sound ki duniya hamare sunne se kaafi badi hai. Insaan lagbhag 20 Hz se 20 kHz tak ki awaaz sun sakta hai (audible range). Usse zyada frequency wali ultrasound ko hum sun nahi paate, par chamgaadar, dolphin aur SONAR jaisi machine use sunti hain aur mapti hain. Usse kam frequency wali infrasound bhi hamare kaanon ke liye nahi hai.\n\nAb ek sawaal bacha hai: **hum sunte kaise hain?** Hawa mein chalti hui sound wave hamare sir ke andar ek electric message mein kaise badalti hai, jise dimaag \"awaaz\" samajhta hai? Aur agar kaan itna nazuk yantra hai, to bahut tez shor (noise) se uska kya hota hai? Ye chapter ka aakhri topic hai, to end mein poore chapter ka wrap-up bhi hoga.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Pichle topic mein humne dekha ki sound ki duniya hamare sunne se kaafi badi hai. Insaan lagbhag 20 Hz se 20 kHz tak ki awaaz sun sakta hai (audible range). Usse zyada frequency wali ultrasound ko hum sun nahi paate, par chamgaadar, dolphin aur SONAR jaisi machine use sunti hain aur mapti hain. Usse kam frequency wali infrasound bhi hamare kaanon ke liye nahi hai.\n\nAb ek sawaal bacha hai: **hum sunte kaise hain?** Hawa mein chalti hui sound wave hamare sir ke andar ek electric message mein kaise badalti hai, jise dimaag \"awaaz\" samajhta hai? Aur agar kaan itna nazuk yantra hai, to bahut tez shor (noise) se uska kya hota hai? Ye chapter ka aakhri topic hai, to end mein poore chapter ka wrap-up bhi hoga."
